The Antigravity package references two third-party projects for the behaviour
of `agy acp`. No source file of either is included.

chengdidididi/agy-acp2api, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 chengdidididi:
the stripped custom agent with a tool-denying hook, the text tool-call
convention, the `_meta.antigravity.systemPrompt.append` system text and the
`-low`, `-medium` and `-high` model variants. Its credential copying into a
second profile, traffic redirection, `SSH_CONNECTION` override, HTTP gateway
and reporting of errors as assistant text are not used.

DylanLIiii/magpie-plugins, package agy-cli, MIT License:
placing the agent under `.agents/agents/` of the working directory so `agy`
keeps its own profile, the 112 KiB replay budget below `agy`'s prompt limit,
the session options for models and thought levels, and the in-band failure
marker. Its MCP bridge through `--ide-mcp-port` is not used.

